<Layout title="Privacy | Trustora" description="Trustora's plain-language privacy notice." currentPath="/legal/privacy/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Legal / Privacy</SectionLabel><h1>A clear note on privacy.</h1><p>Last updated: August 21, 2026. This site is intentionally simple and does not use analytics, advertising, or chat scripts.</p></div><div class="page-hero-note">If you contact Trustora, your message is used to respond to your inquiry and handled by the people responsible for that conversation.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure legal-layout"><aside><SectionLabel>Privacy notice</SectionLabel></aside><div class="prose"><h2>What this site collects</h2><p>Trustora does not intentionally collect personal information merely because you browse this website. The site does not use advertising cookies, analytics scripts, or third-party chat tools.</p><h2>When you contact us</h2><p>If you choose to email Trustora or submit a form, you may provide your name, work email, company, country, role, and the context you choose to share. We use that information to respond to your request and decide whether a conversation is appropriate.</p><h2>When you apply for a career role</h2><p>The careers intake may collect your name and preferred name; email and optional phone or WhatsApp; country or region, city or region, time zone, and professional languages; the role or problem you want to work on and related interests; work authorization, work model, availability, travel or relocation, and scheduling context; education and field; compensation currency and expectation; links to a CV, LinkedIn, GitHub, portfolio, or publications; work evidence and a cover note; and your consent to career-application review. The form also sends submission context such as source, business unit, schema version, and application identifier so the intake can route the request and prevent duplicates.</p><p>When configured, the submission is sent to Trustora's careers intake service. The service uses an Azure Function and Dataverse to receive, validate, route, and manage career-application records for application evaluation and intake operations. Access is limited to the people and systems that need the information for those purposes. Azure, Dataverse, and other vendors may process the information across borders where applicable to the service configuration and operations. Trustora keeps career-applicant information only for as long as it is needed for those purposes or required by law; this notice does not promise a fixed retention period.</p><p>Submitting an application does not promise a role. For questions about career-applicant information, including access, correction, or deletion requests, email <a href="mailto:info@trustora.net">info@trustora.net</a> and identify the request as a privacy matter. Trustora may need to verify your identity and may retain information where required by law or needed for a documented operational purpose.</p><h2>What not to send</h2><p>Please do not send passport details, payroll records, government identifiers, health information, or other sensitive personal information through this website.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@trustora.net">info@trustora.net</a>.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
